  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1155 PM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nThursday-Monday, another shortwave to drop south in the northwest \nflow aloft on Thursday. Guidance continues to show largely dry \nconditions through the day Thursday, but areas east of the \nMississippi River will have the potential for brief light precip.\nLooking at the environment, we are generally looking at isolated\nto widely scattered showers passing through the cyclonic flow \noverhead. Although, this is low confidence and PoPs remain <15%.\nOur higher confidence is with the cooler air that will advect \nin through Thursday, keeping temperatures near to slightly below\nnormal through Saturday. High temperatures are expected to drop\ninto the low- mid 40s, with nights in the 20s to around 30. A \nlarge area of high pressure builds over the region through the \nweekend, slowly tracking east into next week. While overhead, \ntemperatures will remain near seasonal normals with light winds \nand dry conditions. As this tracks east into next week, \ntemperatures will return to above seasonal normals, roughly in \nthe 50s early next week. Dry conditions are currently expected \nto remain through the start of next week, owing to lacking \nmoisture return.",
